<para id="RM0000005RT01MX" category="J" type-id="303AK" name-id="9517G-01" from="200912">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>CAN Bus Main Wire Open Circuit Inspection (DLC3 Branch Wire/Main Wire/Terminating Resistor)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005RT01MX_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AN00001">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>If the resistance between 6 (CANH) and 14 (CANL) of DLC3 is 70 Ω or higher, an open circuit in the CAN bus main line and the DLC3 branch line is suspected.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.54in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.54in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Suspected Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Resistance between 6 (CANH) and 14 (CANL) of DLC3 is 70 Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>CAN bus main line open circuit or connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>DLC3 branch line open circuit or connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>CAN J/C</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer (EFI ECU)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Combination Meter Assembly (Meter ECU)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005RT01MX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AO00001">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162442J02" width="7.106578999in" height="8.799559038in"/>
</figure>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162443J02" width="7.106578999in" height="8.799559038in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>2WD models equipped with neither pre-crash safety nor radar cruise control have no CAN gateway ECU wiring.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005RT01MX_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005RT01MX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000005RT01MX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AP00001">
<testtitle>Inspect DLC3</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09843-18040</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using the SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of DLC3 with the IG OFF.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="I103137J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="4" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.04in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>6(CANH) - 14(CANL)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>108 to 132Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>6(CANH) - 14(CANL)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>133 Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>If CAN communication system DTCs are output when the measurement result is 133 Ω or higher, there may be a malfunction other than an open in the DLC3 branch wire; therefore, after repairing the malfunctioning area, perform troubleshooting again from "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001R4W019X"/>).</ptxt>
</atten3>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000005RT01MX_04_0021" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000005RT01MX_04_0038" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
